### =====================================================================
### appointMe - requests.http  (Days 5-6)
### Run each request with the green arrow next to it, top to bottom.
### Write down the status code you get and compare with "EXPECTED".
### =====================================================================

### Variables - edit if your ids differ (check: SELECT id, name FROM tenants;)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@tenantId = 1
@otherTenantId = 2
@serviceId = 1


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### TENANTS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### T1. Create tenant            EXPECTED: 201 (note the id in the response)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Barber",
  "slug": "test-barber",
  "timezone": "Europe/Athens"
}

> {% client.global.set("newTenantId", response.body.id); %}

### T2. Get tenant               EXPECTED: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}

### T3. Get missing tenant       EXPECTED: 500 now, 404 after Day 7
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/9999

### T4. Duplicate slug           EXPECTED: 500 now, 409 after Day 7
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another Barber",
  "slug": "test-barber",
  "timezone": "Europe/Athens"
}

### T5. Slug with capitals/space EXPECTED: 400 (pattern check)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Slug",
  "slug": "Test Barber",
  "timezone": "UTC"
}

### T6. Blank name               EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "slug": "no-name",
  "timezone": "UTC"
}

### T7. Invalid time zone        EXPECTED: error (400 after Day 7)
###     Works only if you did the ZoneId.of() exercise.
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mars Barber",
  "slug": "mars-barber",
  "timezone": "Mars/Base"
}

### T8. Second tenant (for the isolation test)   EXPECTED: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Second Gym",
  "slug": "second-gym",
  "timezone": "Europe/London"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SERVICES (Day 6)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### S1. Valid create             EXPECTED: 201 (note the service id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": 25.00
}

> {% client.global.set("newServiceId", response.body.id); %}

### S2. Blank name              EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": 25.00
}

### S3. Negative duration       EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": -5,
  "price": 25.00
}

### S4. Missing price          EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 30
}

### S5. Negative price         EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "price": -1
}

### S6. Missing duration       EXPECTED: 400 (this is why the field is Integer, not int)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "price": 25.00
}

### S7. List services          EXPECTED: 200, array
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services

### S8. Get one service       EXPECTED: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### S9. Get missing service    EXPECTED: 500 now, 404 after Day 7
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/9999

### S10. Update (change price) EXPECTED: 200, new price in the body
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Haircut",
  "durationMinutes": 45,
  "price": 30.00,
  "active": true
}

### S11. Delete (soft)        EXPECTED: 204, row stays with active = false
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### S12. List after delete    EXPECTED: 200 (inactive one still shown unless you did the active-filter exercise)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### ISOLATION CHECK
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### I1. Read tenant A's service through tenant B's URL
###     EXPECTED: NOT the data (500 now, 404 after Day 7)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### I2. Update tenant A's service through tenant B's URL
###     EXPECTED: NOT found, and the service stays unchanged
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hacked",
  "durationMinutes": 1,
  "price": 0.00,
  "active": true
}

### I3. Delete tenant A's service through tenant B's URL
###     EXPECTED: NOT found, and active stays true
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### EXTRA EXPERIMENTS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### X1. Try to sneak in an id   EXPECTED: 201, but the id in the body is ignored
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 99,
  "name": "Sneaky",
  "slug": "sneaky",
  "timezone": "UTC"
}

### X2. Empty body             EXPECTED: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### X3. Missing Content-Type   EXPECTED: 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants

{"name":"x","slug":"x"}
